    "summary": "Review of direct check 7815ca48454b4d919a20810718683b41 (unit-claim-timeout-now-attribution), preflight-validated with valid=True and no diagnostics.\n\nFresh execution 554a0abcf056483ba255f00545e30713 completed the comparison: the declarative prerequisite unattributed-sender matched, comparison_complete and witness_complete are true at witness index 1, and the implication evaluated false. The unattributed TimeoutNow (sender absent from the receiver's bootstrapped two-voter configuration) was honoured — leader node2 cleared, state Follower to Candidate, privilege false to true, no error — exactly like the configured-sender control, while the out-of-window control was rejected with 'operation not supported with current protocol version' and changed nothing, showing the version window is the only guard on this path.\n\nProduct contents: the required checker_correspondence item (no_issue_found, empty counterevidence) covering requirement versus predicate, caller duties, identity/correlation, the event-based oracle (exit 0 while the implication is false), completion, and disclosed limitations; an applicability item; and resolutions for the two open issues add89d8bab1d42fe9bd4d7c04645bf4b (claim) and ec03c9c6d31b42e4a5652992c7c8bc59 (harness legality), both disposing the documentation-versus-handler condition as independent_scope with sources.\n\nExplicitly retained, not hidden: the unattributed sender is a fabricated identifier, so the check establishes the handler's decision for such a sender rather than that a removed running node reaches it; nodes run without background goroutines, so term interaction and the subsequent election are not exercised; the consequence for a healthy leader is unmeasured; and the reading of the LeadershipTransfer documentation in mixed-version clusters is kept as an open boundary rather than used to weaken the claim. Three in-scope violations are now recorded as comparisons (batching-FSM ConfigurationStore delivery, heartbeat fast-path header gate, and TimeoutNow sender attribution), the first two already confirmed."
